 "bloques": [
  {
   "tipo": "explicacion",
   "titulo": "Gustar: «gostar de»",
   "texto": [
    "In Portuguese «gustar» does not work as in Spanish. The person is the subject, as in «yo adoro», and what he likes always goes with **de**: **Gosto de café** = I like coffee (literally, «I like coffee.»).",
    "It is conjugated like any verb in -ar: gust, gust, gourmet, gourmet, gourmet.",
    "**Gostas de peixe?** = Do you like fish? **Não gosto de carne** = I don't like meat. **Gosto muito** = I like it a lot."
   ]
  },
  {
   "tipo": "explicacion",
   "titulo": "With verbs",
   "texto": [
    "Also with **de**: **Gosto de cozinhar** (I like cooking), **gosto de comer** (I like eating).",
    "Other verbs of taste, these without «de»: **adoro** (I love), **detesto** (hate) and **prefiro** (I prefer)."
   ]
  },
